# WITHOUT THIS FILE, `COPY . /home/agent/agent` PUT THE OPERATOR'S API KEYS
# IN THE IMAGE.
#
# docker-compose.yml and the README both tell the owner to fill in agent.env
# BEFORE building. The Dockerfile then copied the whole build context — so
# the image carried agent.env (world-readable at 0755), the entire .git
# history, 230 MB of deploy/worker/node_modules, the developer's trained
# experts, and every test sandbox. Pushing that image to any registry
# publishes the keys.
#
# Every other guard against shipping a secret — .gitignore, package.py's
# credential scan, the CI archive assertion — lives on a different layer.
# The docker build context had none of them, which is the same shape as
# every other defect found in this project's deployment audit: a guard at
# one layer, and the layer around it bare.

# --- credentials, first and non-negotiable -------------------------------
agent.env
*.env
!agent.env.example
ui-token.txt
keys/
.keys/
secrets/
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
federation/identity.json

# --- this fleet's memory: someone else's image must not carry it ---------
experts/
commons/
org/
logs/
contexts/
backups/
inbox/
proof/observations/
demo-run/
demo-run.prev-*
state.json
briefing.md
commons-digest.md

# --- weight, not danger ---------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
deploy/worker/node_modules/
tests/tmp/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.zip
docs/panel/*.png
